**output**
**build**
**tmp**
**secret**
**private**
**key**
**local**

# Claude Code: .claude/settings.json is shared and tracked; a person's own
# overrides and agent worktrees are not. CLAUDE.local.md holds host-specific
# agent notes (the blanket **local** above already matches both local files;
# named here so the intent survives that rule going).
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
CLAUDE.local.md

*.js
*.ts
*.bat
*.cmd
*.ps
*.ps1
*.ps2
*.psd
*.doc
*.docx
*.id
*.py
*.pyc
*.pem
*.pub
*.env
*.direnv
*.envrc
*.rsa
*.crt
*.pfx
*.bmp
*.cert
*.key
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.log
*.txt
# setup-tool's roster, which the blanket *.txt above would swallow; the action
# and the drift checker both read it
!.github/actions/setup-tool/tools.txt
# the drift checker's repo hook, which the blanket **local** above would swallow
!.github/scripts/check_tool_versions.local.sh
*.tsv
*.csv
*.sql
*.toml
# the typos allowlist, read by the lint gate (tests/lint/tools_test.sh)
!.typos.toml
!.moxide.toml
# lychee's link-check config, read by ci.yml and link-check.yml
!lychee.toml
# everything under the payload directories ships, whatever it is named: the
# blanket rules above once swallowed a settings/*.toml (drift_test.sh's
# lint_ignored_payload keeps it that way)
!settings/**
!common/**
# packaging/mkpkg.sh's staging and output directory. Not "build/" or
# "output/": the blanket rules above would swallow those.
dist/

# this project's own publishing keys
!packaging/apk/*.rsa.pub

# npm installs of the pinned CI Markdown tools (.github/package.json)
node_modules/
